    "$comment": "Reference normalization, read by both languages. The declared Reference requires one of ref/url/uri, so an entry carrying nothing must be dropped rather than emitted empty. `refs` is spliced into a control verbatim and `want` is the normalized array. These lived inline in the Go suite and asserted only a count, with no TypeScript twin at all \u2014 which is how the empty-ref defect reached one language and not the other.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "a string ref becomes a ref object",
        "refs": [
          "NIST SP 800-53"
        ],
        "want": [
          {
            "ref": "NIST SP 800-53"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "an empty string carries nothing",
